      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s a problem here. If we timeout from the SNK_TRANSITION state and go back to the SNK_DISCOVERY state, then there is no more PD_T_SINK_WAIT_CAP timeout set for going to HARD_RESET. So, we would just stay in SNK_DISCOVERY forever.\n\nI like where this is going... maybe we need a set_state_timeout() function that is called directly from the state which is setting a timeout. I think it would be more clear with these states to have state entry conditions. For example, the discovery state could look like:\n\ncase PD_STATE_SNK_DISCOVERY:\n  /* On state entry, set source cap expired timeout */\n  if (last_state !\u003d pd[port].task_state)\n    set_state_timeout(get_time().val + PD_T_SINK_WAIT_CAP,\n                      HARD_RESET);\n  break;\n\nYes, it does mean adding a var to keep track of last state, but I think it is much more clear when the state that is waiting for a timeout has the timeout code in it.",
